1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:07,538
This curved steel hall spans twenty meters: two hundred fourteen nodes, four hundred forty three frames and one hundred zinc panels.

2
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:16,622
The same model went into four programs with the same mesh, the same nodes and the same loads, so what is compared are the solvers, not the load paths.

3
00:00:16,870 --> 00:00:25,774
In the first mode Hekatan Struct gives a period of zero point three three one one four four seconds, and SAP two thousand gives the same number to the sixth digit.

4
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:33,244
ETABS stays within two hundredths of a percent, but only after turning on its vertical mass, which ships disabled.

5
00:00:33,490 --> 00:00:40,090
OpenSees lands within a quarter of a percent, and that gap is not the solver: its shell is a different element.

6
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:46,580
Four independent programs, the same hall and the same number: that is what validation means.

